\begin{abstract}
We present a unified numerical simulation engine capable of evolving
General Relativity (BSSN/ADM 3+1 formalism), relativistic hydrodynamics,
cosmic expansion (FLRW), thermodynamic phase transitions, deterministic
chaos, and semiclassical quantum vacuum perturbations within a single
computational framework. The system employs strict double precision,
high-order finite-difference and finite-volume methods, adaptive mesh
refinement (AMR), and post-quantum cryptographic data ingestion. We
demonstrate fourth-order convergence, constraint preservation, shock
capturing fidelity, and empirical agreement with observational datasets
including Gaia DR3, JWST UNCOVER, Planck PR4, and LIGO GWTC-3.
\end{abstract}

